! v0.73.0 PCM test 2:  water in DMSO (HF/STO-3G, C-PCM).
!
! DMSO (epsilon = 46.83) is significantly less polar than water
! (epsilon = 78.36); the polarization free energy should be smaller in
! magnitude than test 1 because f(eps) = (eps - 1) / eps is smaller
! (0.979 in DMSO vs 0.987 in water -- only ~1% difference, but this
! is a useful regression that the solvent-name lookup is wired up).
!
! Sanity check: |G_pol(DMSO)| < |G_pol(water)| at the same geometry.
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%pcm     cpcm     ! v0.74+ default is iefpcm; v0.73 tests pin cpcm explicitly
%solvent dmso
%geom angstrom
O  0.000000   0.000000   0.119262
H  0.000000   0.755453  -0.477047
H  0.000000  -0.755453  -0.477047
*end
